      "media": [],
      "hasMediaInOriginal": false,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "ITALY TAKES A STAND AGAINST ANTISEMITISM\n\nHere in Rome, Italy’s parliament has given final approval to a bill aimed at combating antisemitism. Backed by Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni’s coalition, it passed the lower house on Tuesday - 147 in favor, 93 against and five abstentions.\n\nThe legislation incorporates the International Holocaust Remembrance Alliance’s working definition of antisemitism. Depending on the context, denying the Jewish people their right to self-determination or applying double standards to Israel can be antisemitic.\n\nOpponents argued that the measure could restrict free speech and advocacy for Palestinians. Meloni’s coalition said legitimate criticism of Israeli government policy remains protected.\n\nI welcome this vote. Hatred of Jews is still hatred of Jews, even when it’s dressed up as “anti-Zionism.” Italy is right to say so clearly.",
